prompt.text:
Implement a self-contained TypeScript module exporting a `ChannelHub` class:

```ts
export type ChannelListener<T> = (payload: T) => void;

export class ChannelHub<T> {
  attach(channel: string, listener: ChannelListener<T>): number;
  detach(channel: string, token: number): boolean;
  clear(channel: string): number;
  publish(channel: string, payload: T): number;
}
```

Channel names must be non-empty after trimming; invalid names throw `TypeError`. The original, untrimmed name is the identity of a valid channel. `attach` returns a positive token unique within the hub. Duplicate listener functions are separate registrations. `detach` removes only the registration matching both channel and token and reports whether it existed. `clear` removes all listeners for a channel and returns the number removed. Publishing an unknown channel returns zero.

Listeners run synchronously in registration order. `publish` returns the number invoked. It must use a snapshot: attachments and removals made during publication affect only later publications. If a listener throws, stop immediately and propagate that error. Payloads are passed through unchanged. No method may expose or mutate a caller-owned collection.

